Medical Terminology 2e — Open RN (@med-source-terminology: 0, is #book, #part-of @medicine-sources) { r_6R6B3VDJ3NYF8QKGJYBZTSTT3Q
Open Resources for Nursing, Open RN; edited by Kimberly Ernstmeyer and Elizabeth Christman. Medical Terminology, 2nd edition. Chippewa Valley Technical College/WisTech Open, 2024. English. Ebook ISBN 9781957068060.

[Publisher edition](https://wtcs.pressbooks.pub/medterm/) · [NCBI Bookshelf](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK607454/) · [Download PDF](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK607454/pdf/Bookshelf_NBK607454.pdf).

**Substantial first reading:** chapters 1–2 in full, including the written activities and glossaries. Later read chapters 13–14 in full for skeletal and muscular terminology, and the relevant parts of chapter 16 for nervous-system language. All 17 chapters form an optional whole-book reading across medical fields. This is a terminology textbook with anatomical and clinical context, not a substitute for the main anatomy and physiology book or a treatment reference.

The NCBI PDF has 996 file pages and preserves the 2024 edition notices. Printed pagination differs. Some interactive activities and videos require the linked web edition; the PDF explains their absence. Use the [NCBI-hosted PDF](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK607454/pdf/Bookshelf_NBK607454.pdf) for offline reading.

**Access and reuse:** copyright 2024 Open RN/WisTech Open; CC BY 4.0 except where otherwise noted. Credit the title, contributors, edition, publisher, and source, and preserve component notices. [Licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

